<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=cotton">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Tools and materials</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cotton</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cotton is a plant fibre spun and woven into textiles, one of the most important traded commodities in history. Indian cotton textiles were exported widely under the Gupta, Mughal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> empires, and cotton was cultivated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>. In the industrial era, cotton manufacturing was central to the economy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cotton.jpg" alt="Cotton" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: കാക്കര · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cotton_-_%E0%B4%AA%E0%B4%B0%E0%B5%81%E0%B4%A4%E0%B5%8D%E0%B4%A4%E0%B4%BF_03.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Pastoral clans moved their herds between dry-season wells and wet-season pastures, while farmers along the Shabelle grew sorghum, maize in later centuries, beans and <b>cotton</b>, partly with the help of canals and floodwater.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ajuran-sultanate">Ajuran Sultanate · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>In return, Aksum imported textiles, glassware, wine, olive oil and metalwork from the Mediterranean world, and spices, <b>cotton</b> and gems from India.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>As late as 1930, Hamaj villagers in the southern Gezira would swear by 'Soba the home of my grandfathers and grandmothers which can make the stone float and the <b>cotton</b> ball sink'.</blockquote><a href="/empire/alodia">Alodia · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>It traded in spices, hides, wool and <b>cotton</b> and exported timber, grain, wine and raw silk.</blockquote><a href="/empire/armenian-kingdom-of-cilicia">Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>About 54.9 percent of the land is agricultural, growing grain, <b>cotton</b>, tobacco, potatoes and sugar beet, with wine, livestock and a Caspian sturgeon fishery; tourism, damaged by the war of the 1990s, recovered in the 2000s.</blockquote><a href="/empire/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Beyond the valley, the 38 tribute provinces recorded in the Codex Mendoza supplied <b>cotton</b>, cacao, precious feathers, gold dust, jaguar skins and countless other goods.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
